   "stem": "Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium depends on five key assumptions: no mutation, no migration, random mating, a very large population (no genetic drift), and no natural selection. For EACH of these five assumptions, explain specifically how violating it would change allele frequencies in a real population, and give one brief example of each violation. (Long Answer) TECHNOLOGY AND TECHNIQUES",
