   "explanation": "",
   "sample": "Accept responses that describe, in detail: Initiation — RNA polymerase binds to the promoter, a specific DNA sequence located upstream of the gene, causing the DNA double helix to locally unwind and expose the template strand. Elongation — RNA polymerase moves along the template strand, synthesizing a complementary RNA strand in the 5’ to 3’ direction (reading the template 3’ to 5’), pairing each DNA base with its RNA complement (A with U, T with A, G with C, C with G). Termination — RNA polymerase reaches the terminator sequence, which signals it to stop transcribing, release the completed RNA transcript, and detach from the DNA. The resulting RNA transcript is complementary and antiparallel to the DNA template strand it was copied from (and matches the sequence of the non-template/coding strand, except with U in place of T), once Image 7 is inserted. POPULATION & EVOLUTIONARY GENETICS",
